      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Let’s be honest: VRChat will probably never do anything about this.\n\nNot because they aren’t aware of it. Not because they haven’t seen the posts. Not because they’re just now finding out that Shadow PC or cloud gaming users are getting blocked. They already know this very well.\n\nThe real problem is that we clearly don’t represent enough users for this to become a priority. With a few thousand upvotes, maybe they’d at least bother to respond. But as things stand, the silence is already an answer.\n\nAnd as for EAC, we also need to stop acting as if it were all some incomprehensible technical inevitability. Ever since Shadow PC and other cloud PCs have been blocked, it’s pretty clear that developers know exactly what they’re doing. Games that block VMs or cloud PCs generally do so intentionally, for reasons of security, anti-cheat measures, moderation, to prevent ban circumvention, or simply because they don’t want to deal with that scenario.\n\nAnd conversely, if a game decides to allow them, it’s not magic either: it’s also a deliberate decision.\n\nSo yes, VRChat could at least clarify its position. They could clearly state: \"We do not wish to support Shadow PC or cloud/VM environments for such-and-such a reason\". They don’t even do that.\n\nIt’s frustrating, but we need to stop believing that they’re just waiting for “the right moment” to change their minds. They’ve already had plenty of time to respond. They’re simply choosing not to..",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
